{
  "summary": "The app’s UI largely follows DESIGN.md – every screen listed in the spec exists, the primary flow runs without errors, and axe reports no accessibility violations (accessibility score 98%). The Material‑3 theme is applied to most components and the bottom‑tab navigation and FAB are reachable from every screen. However, several medium‑severity gaps were found: missing validation on numeric fields and backup passphrase length, incomplete sanitisation for CSV/PDF export, a missing CSP meta‑tag for the web build, leftover temporary backup files, no image‑size limits on receipt photos, the encryption key is not cleared on a full data wipe, and some components still use hard‑coded spacing / colour values instead of the design tokens. Focus‑visible styling is also absent on a few interactive elements (MiniFAB, switch toggles). These issues don’t break the primary flow but they affect security, consistency with the design system and full keyboard accessibility.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase modal only checks for non‑empty input; it does not enforce the required minimum length (8 characters) or the three‑of‑four character‑class rule defined in the design spec.",
      "fix": "Add validation logic that checks the passphrase length and character‑class composition before enabling the \"Create backup\" button, and display a HelperText error when the policy is not met."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Numeric fields (Amount) lack robust validation – negative numbers, zero or non‑numeric strings can be entered, and there is no upper‑bound check.",
      "fix": "Validate that amount > 0, enforce a sensible maximum (e.g., < 1 000 000), and show a HelperText error. Disable the Save button until the field is valid."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Mileage Miles field and Mileage Rate (in TaxSettingsScreen) accept any string; no validation for numeric range or positivity.",
      "fix": "Add client‑side validation that ensures miles ≥ 0 and rate > 0, with appropriate HelperText messages and disabled Save until valid."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/exportCsv.ts",
      "issue": "CSV export does not consistently sanitise fields that start with '=', '+', '-', or '@', opening the app to formula injection in spreadsheets.",
      "fix": "Implement a sanitisation routine that prefixes a single quote to any such field or wraps all fields in double‑quotes with proper escaping before joining rows."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/exportPdf.ts",
      "issue": "PDF generation builds an HTML template by interpolating user‑provided text (notes, categories) without HTML‑escaping, risking script injection in PDF viewers.",
      "fix": "Escape all user data using a vetted library (e.g., `escape-html`) before embedding into the HTML string used for PDF creation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "public/index.html",
      "issue": "The optional web build lacks a Content‑Security‑Policy header/meta tag, exposing the page to injection attacks.",
      "fix": "Add `<meta http-equiv=\"Content‑Security‑Policy\" content=\"default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:;\">` or configure the hosting server to emit an equivalent CSP header."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/backup.ts",
      "issue": "After a successful share of the encrypted backup, the temporary file created for `expo-sharing` is never deleted, leaving residual data on the device.",
      "fix": "Call `FileSystem.deleteAsync(tmpPath, { idempotent: true })` after `shareAsync` resolves, and optionally overwrite the file before deletion."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/photoPicker.ts",
      "issue": "Receipt photo picker does not enforce a maximum image size or resolution, allowing users to select arbitrarily large images that can exhaust device storage.",
      "fix": "Configure `expo-image-picker` with a `quality` or `maxWidth`/`maxHeight` option, and reject or downscale images that exceed a safe size threshold."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/dataReset.ts",
      "issue": "The \"Delete all data\" flow clears the SQLite tables but does not delete the encryption key stored in SecureStore, leaving encrypted remnants recoverable.",
      "fix": "When performing a full data wipe, also call `SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(KEY_NAME)` to remove the key and optionally wipe the DB file."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Component styles use hard‑coded values (e.g., `marginBottom: 16`, `borderRadius: 8`) instead of the design token values (`theme.spacing`, `theme.roundness`).",
      "fix": "Replace literal numbers with token references, e.g., `marginBottom: theme.spacing * 2`, `borderRadius: theme.roundness`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Uses explicit padding (`padding: 16`) and elevation (`elevation: 1`) rather than pulling from the theme’s spacing and elevation objects.",
      "fix": "Refactor to use `theme.spacing * 2` for padding and `theme.elevation.level1` for elevation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "MiniFAB does not provide a visible focus ring for keyboard navigation; only the large FAB has focus‑visible styling.",
      "fix": "Add a 2 dp outline using the theme’s `outline` colour when the MiniFAB receives focus (e.g., via `onFocus` style)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The `PrimaryButton` component lacks `autocomplete` attributes for forms that contain password fields (e.g., backup passphrase), which can improve keyboard usability.",
      "fix": "Pass through `autoComplete` prop from the parent `FormField` or expose it on the button if needed for password visibility toggles."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "FormField does not set appropriate `autoComplete` attributes for numeric inputs (e.g., amount, miles) or for secure fields (passphrase).",
      "fix": "Add `autoComplete='off'` for numeric fields and `autoComplete='new-password'` for passphrase fields, and expose a prop to customize the attribute."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/MiniFAB.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing `accessibilityLabel` on the MiniFAB icons, which could cause screen‑reader users to be unaware of the button’s purpose.",
      "fix": "Add an `accessibilityLabel` prop (e.g., \"Add receipt\" / \"Add mileage\") to each MiniFAB."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "Tab icons are decorative but the `accessibilityLabel` is set only on the navigation container; individual tabs lack `accessibilityState` for the selected state.",
      "fix": "Ensure each tab item includes `accessibilityState={{ selected: true }}` when active, and `accessibilityLabel` describing the destination."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/CheckboxField.tsx",
      "issue": "Checkboxes use `Checkbox.Android`/`Checkbox.IOS` without explicit `accessibilityRole='checkbox'` which might be missing on web.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole='checkbox'` and ensure the `accessibilityState` reflects `checked`/`unchecked`."
    }
  ]
}

