{
  "summary": "The UI passes most accessibility checks but the end‑to‑end primary flow breaks at the backup step – the success snackbar and share sheet never appear, preventing users from completing the backup use‑case. In addition, critical security hardening required by the design (CSV sanitisation, HTML‑escaping for PDF, strong backup‑passphrase enforcement) is still missing, which could expose users to data‑exfiltration or injection attacks. Several medium‑severity issues also remain (web CSP, image‑size validation, encryption‑key cleanup on data‑reset, and the deletion‑key persistence bug). Minor style/markup inconsistencies are found but do not block the flow.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup flow never shows the success snackbar or triggers the native share sheet after creating the encrypted backup, causing the UI flow test to time‑out at \"Backup ready to share\".",
      "fix": "Ensure the backup library resolves successfully and then call `shareAsync` followed by `Snackbar.show({ message: \"Backup ready to share.\" })`. Add proper error handling to show the error snackbar if sharing fails."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/lib/exportCsv.ts",
      "issue": "CSV export concatenates raw user data without sanitising leading characters, leaving the app vulnerable to CSV/Formula injection attacks.",
      "fix": "Sanitise every field before joining: prefix a single quote (`'`) if the field starts with `=`, `+`, `-`, or `@`, or wrap all fields in double quotes and escape internal quotes. Add unit tests for injection cases."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/lib/exportPdf.ts",
      "issue": "PDF export builds an HTML string by interpolating user‑provided fields directly, opening the possibility of HTML/script injection in PDF viewers.",
      "fix": "Escape all interpolated user data using a robust HTML‑escaping library (e.g., `escape-html`). Ensure the template only contains sanitized data and add tests covering malicious input."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The policy‑gate error state (full‑screen with Retry button) is not implemented – the UI only shows a loading indicator and the agreement UI, so a storage failure cannot be recovered.",
      "fix": "Add an error view component that displays the copy \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" with a Retry button that re‑invokes the acceptance store operation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Touch target size is set to `>=44×44dp` only for the button height (48dp) but the width can shrink below the required 44dp when the label is short, violating the minimum tap area.",
      "fix": "Force a minimum width of 44dp (or use `style={{ minWidth: 44 }}`) on the button component to guarantee the required tap area on all platforms."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase UI only checks for matching fields and a minimum length; it does not enforce the required three‑of‑four character‑class rule, allowing weak passwords.",
      "fix": "Add validation that checks for at least 8 characters and the presence of three character classes (uppercase, lowercase, digit, symbol). Disable the Create backup button until the rule passes and show a HelperText error if not."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "public/index.html",
      "issue": "Web fallback lacks a Content‑Security‑Policy header/meta tag, exposing the app to injection attacks when run in a browser.",
      "fix": "Add a CSP meta tag or configure the web server to send an HTTP CSP header restricting sources to `'self'` for scripts, styles, images, etc."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/photoPicker.ts",
      "issue": "Receipt photo picker accepts arbitrarily large image files; large images can exhaust device storage or cause OOM crashes.",
      "fix": "Limit the picker options (`quality`, `allowsEditing`, `maxWidth`/`maxHeight`) and after selection validate the file size, rejecting or down‑scaling images that exceed a safe threshold (e.g., >5 MB)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/dataReset.ts",
      "issue": "Delete‑all‑data action clears SQLite tables but does not delete the encryption key stored in `expo-secure-store`, leaving encrypted remnants potentially recoverable.",
      "fix": "After clearing the database, also call `SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(KEY_NAME)` to remove the encryption key, and optionally wipe the raw database file."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/backup.ts",
      "issue": "Temporary backup file created for sharing is never deleted after a successful share, leaving the encrypted blob on the device.",
      "fix": "Invoke `FileSystem.deleteAsync(tmpPath, { idempotent: true })` after `shareAsync` resolves (or in a finally block) to clean up the temporary file."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/storage/device.web.ts",
      "issue": "Encryption key is persisted in `localStorage` for the optional web build, which is insecure.",
      "fix": "Derive the key from the user‑provided passphrase each session (e.g., using PBKDF2/scrypt) instead of persisting it, or store it in IndexedDB with proper encryption."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/exportCsv.ts",
      "issue": "Numeric fields (amount, miles) are not rounded/validated before export, which can produce malformed CSV rows.",
      "fix": "Validate and format numeric values to a fixed decimal precision (e.g., two decimal places) before adding them to the CSV output."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The `actionLabel` prop is rendered as plain text without a button role or explicit `accessibilityRole=\"button\"`, making it less discoverable for screen readers.",
      "fix": "Render the action as a `PrimaryButton` (or `<Button>`) with appropriate `accessibilityLabel` and role, ensuring keyboard focus and announcement."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FAB icons lack `accessibilityLabel` attributes, so screen readers cannot convey their purpose (Receipt vs Mileage).",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Add mileage\"` to the respective MiniFAB components."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible outline is applied only on web via CSS; native platforms do not show a visible focus indicator, which may affect keyboard navigation on TV/desktop environments.",
      "fix": "Add a native focus ring using `react-native-paper`’s `rippleColor` or a custom `borderWidth` style when `focused` prop is true, mirroring the web outline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The `Screen` wrapper uses a regular `ScrollView` without `keyboardShouldPersistTaps=\"handled\"`, causing inputs to lose focus when tapping outside, which can be frustrating.",
      "fix": "Set `keyboardShouldPersistTaps=\"handled\"` on the `ScrollView` to keep the keyboard open while tapping the screen."
    }
  ]
}

