{
  "summary": "The majority of screens, states and visual tokens are present, but critical gaps break the primary user journey and introduce security and accessibility regressions. The backup flow never shows the expected success Snackbar (\"Backup ready to share\"), causing the end‑to‑end flow to time‑out. CSV and PDF export implementations concatenate user‑provided data without sanitisation, creating high‑severity injection vectors. Numeric entry fields and the backup‑passphrase UI lack required validation and field‑level error feedback, weakening UX and security. Several UI components still use hard‑coded colors, spacing and border‑radius values instead of the design‑token theme, and focus‑visible styles are missing, which compromises visual consistency and WCAG compliance. These high‑ and medium‑severity issues must be resolved before the app can be considered production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "After the user creates a backup the UI never displays the \"Backup ready to share\" Snackbar and does not trigger the native share sheet, causing the primary flow test to timeout.",
      "fix": "Call the Snackbar component with `visible={true}` and `children=\"Backup ready to share\"` after `shareAsync` resolves successfully. Ensure the share sheet promise is awaited before hiding the loading indicator and that the Snackbar is rendered on the same screen (or navigate back to Settings)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/lib/exportCsv.ts",
      "issue": "CSV export builds rows by directly concatenating raw receipt/mileage fields. Cells that start with '=', '+', '-', or '@' are not escaped, exposing the app to CSV/Formula injection attacks.",
      "fix": "Implement a sanitisation routine that prefixes a single quote to any field starting with those characters or, more robustly, wrap every field in double quotes and escape inner quotes (e.g., using `csv-stringify`). Apply the routine to all user‑controlled values before joining rows."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/lib/exportPdf.ts",
      "issue": "PDF export creates an HTML string by interpolating user‑provided data (notes, categories, etc.) without HTML‑escaping, allowing malicious markup or script injection in PDF viewers that render HTML.",
      "fix": "Escape all interpolated values with a proven library such as `escape-html` before inserting them into the PDF template. Consider whitelisting allowed characters and sanitising line breaks."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The backup UI accepts any non‑empty passphrase and does not enforce the required ≥ 8‑character length or three‑of‑four character‑class rule. No HelperText error is shown when the policy fails, and the Create Backup button can be enabled with a weak passphrase.",
      "fix": "Add client‑side validation that checks length ≥ 8 and at least three character classes (uppercase, lowercase, digits, symbols). Show a `HelperText` error like “Passphrases must match and be at least 8 characters with three character classes.” and keep the button disabled until the rule passes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Numeric fields (Amount, Mileage, Tax Rate) lack validation – negative numbers, non‑numeric strings, and excessively large values are accepted, and no field‑level error messages are displayed.",
      "fix": "Validate each numeric input on change: ensure the value is a positive number, enforce a sensible upper bound (e.g., < 1 000 000), and reject non‑numeric characters. Use `HelperText` to show messages (e.g., “Enter a positive amount.”) and keep the Save button disabled until all validations pass."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button styling uses hard‑coded hex colors and fixed dimensions (e.g., `backgroundColor: '#0061A4'`, `height: 48`). This bypasses the Material‑3 theme tokens defined in `src/theme.ts`.",
      "fix": "Replace literal colors with `theme.colors.primary` and `theme.colors.onPrimary`. Use `theme.roundness` for border radius and `theme.spacing` for padding/margins. Pull the height from a token (e.g., `theme.spacing * 6`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Card layout uses literal values for margin, border radius and elevation (`marginBottom: 16`, `borderRadius: 8`, `elevation: 1`). This diverges from the design‑token system.",
      "fix": "Swap literals for `theme.spacing * 2`, `theme.roundness`, and `theme.elevation.level1.elevation`. Reference `theme.elevation.level1.shadowOpacity` for consistency."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No visible focus style is applied for keyboard navigation on web; the button lacks the required 2 dp outline with the `outline` color when focused.",
      "fix": "Add a `focused` style that sets `outlineWidth: 2`, `outlineColor: theme.colors.outline`, and `outlineStyle: 'solid'`. Apply it via `onFocus`/`onBlur` or the `focusVisibleClassName` prop (for web) to match the spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "The BottomNavigation component does not expose an explicit ARIA role or label, so screen readers may not recognize it as a navigation landmark.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"navigation\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Bottom navigation\"` (or `role=\"navigation\"` for the web) to the root component."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The illustration element inside EmptyState lacks an appropriate `role=\"img\"` and `aria-label`, and the primary action button is not announced via an `aria-live` region.",
      "fix": "Wrap the illustration in a view with `role=\"img\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Empty state illustration\"`. Add `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"` to the action button or surrounding container so the button label is announced when the state appears."
    }
  ]
}

