      "fix": "Add a shared ScreenContainer that applies {width:'100%', maxWidth: 640, alignSelf:'center', paddingHorizontal: 24} on width ≥ 768 and vertically centres the card block (justifyContent:'center') while the footer remains pinned to the bottom edge with the same 640px max width.",
      "shared": true
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The screen reads as an unstyled list: oversized page padding, a receipt card whose data is a flat run of label:value lines, no way to add a receipt (the spec's FAB is missing), and a bottom tab bar whose labels are clipped by the safe area. Fixing the card component, the screen padding scale and the tab bar in the theme/shared layer will lift every list screen in the app.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Bottom tab bar (navigation container)",
      "issue": "Tab labels ('Dashboard', 'Receipts', …) are visually cut off at the bottom edge — the bar has no safe-area bottom inset and no fixed height, so it collides with the home indicator area.",
      "fix": "In the tab navigator screenOptions set tabBarStyle={{ height: 56 + insets.bottom, paddingTop: 8, paddingBottom: Math.max(insets.bottom, 8), borderTopWidth: StyleSheet.hairlineWidth, borderTopColor: theme.colors.outlineVariant, backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface }} using useSafeAreaInsets(), and tabBarLabelStyle={{ fontSize: 12, lineHeight: 16 }} (labelMedium). Keep icon size 24.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Add-receipt FAB",
      "issue": "The spec requires the FAB for 'Add receipt' on the Receipts screen, but there is no primary action anywhere on this screen — the user can only add from the dashboard.",
      "fix": "Add <FAB icon=\"plus\" label=\"Add receipt\" onPress={goToReceiptEntry} style={{ position:'absolute', right:16, bottom:16 + insets.bottom }} /> (Paper FAB, variant default, theme primaryContainer). Put it in a shared ScreenFab wrapper so Mileage reuses it, and give the FlatList contentContainerStyle paddingBottom: 96 so the last card is never hidden.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "ReceiptCard content layout",
      "issue": "All four lines are the same visual weight and use debug-style 'Date:' / 'Category:' labels; the amount (the thing users scan for) is only slightly bolder, and the note sits last in near-equal size. No hierarchy.",
      "fix": "Restructure Card.Content into: row 1 = note/merchant text (titleMedium, onSurface) left + amount (titleMedium, 600, onSurface) right; row 2 = '2026-10-10 · Supplies' as a single bodySmall line in onSurfaceVariant (drop the 'Date:'/'Category:' prefixes). Vertical gap 4 between rows, Card.Content padding 16.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Screen content padding / list gutters",
      "issue": "Horizontal padding is ~48px on phone, far off the 16px Material gutter, so the card looks cramped in width and the header does not match other screens.",
      "fix": "In the shared Screen/ScreenContainer component set contentContainerStyle={{ paddingHorizontal: 16, paddingTop: 8 }} and give the FlatList ItemSeparatorComponent of 12px height. Remove per-screen padding overrides.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "'Expense' type indicator",
      "issue": "The entry type is plain blue-grey text that reads like a link and carries no semantic colour, making expense vs income indistinguishable at a glance.",
      "fix": "Replace with a compact <Chip compact mode=\"flat\" textStyle={{fontSize:12, lineHeight:16}}> using theme.colors.errorContainer/onErrorContainer for Expense and tertiaryContainer/onTertiaryContainer for Income; place it in row 2 right side, height 24.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Screen title 'Receipts'",
      "issue": "Rendered as an oversized ad-hoc bold text (~40px) with 48px top inset; on desktop it is centred over the column while the card is left-aligned, so the heading style is inconsistent across breakpoints.",
      "fix": "Use a shared ScreenHeader: <Text variant=\"headlineMedium\"> with paddingHorizontal 16, paddingTop 16, paddingBottom 8, textAlign left at all widths; on desktop wrap list + header in a single container with maxWidth 720, alignSelf 'center', width '100%'.",
      "shared": true
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The screen reads as a stack of identical outlined buttons rather than a settings list: there is no grouping, no icons, no affordance for navigation, a duplicated 'App lock' entry, and the destructive action looks exactly like the others. Converting the body to Paper List sections inside cards (as a shared SettingsList/SettingsRow component), fixing the duplicate row, marking the destructive action, and fixing the clipped tab labels would lift this screen the most.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "element": "Navigation rows (App lock, Tax settings, Export, Backup & restore, Delete all data, View Terms and Privacy Policy)",
      "issue": "Six full-width outlined Buttons with 16px gaps look like a form of equal-weight CTAs, not a settings menu; centered blue labels give no hierarchy, no icons, and no 'navigates to' affordance, and the repeated 1px outlines create visual noise.",
      "fix": "Replace the Buttons with Paper `List.Item` rows inside a shared `SettingsSection` component: `<Surface elevation={0} style={{backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface, borderRadius: 12, overflow:'hidden'}}>` containing `<List.Item title=\"Tax settings\" titleStyle={{...theme.fonts.bodyLarge, color: theme.colors.onSurface}} left={p => <List.Icon {...p} icon=\"calculator-variant-outline\" color={theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant}/>} right={p => <List.Icon {...p} icon=\"chevron-right\" color={theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant}/>} onPress={...} />` with `<Divider leftInset />` between rows, row height 56, horizontal padding 16. Left-align all labels.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "'App lock' duplicate entry",
      "issue": "App lock appears twice — once as a card with a Switch and again as a navigation button directly below it — which is confusing and makes the toggle card look like a stray element.",
      "fix": "Delete the standalone 'App lock' button and merge the toggle into the first list section as `<List.Item title=\"App lock\" description=\"Require biometric authentication on launch\" descriptionNumberOfLines={2} left={p => <List.Icon {...p} icon=\"lock-outline\"/>} right={() => <Switch value={locked} onValueChange={...} />} />`. If App lock has its own detail page, keep only the row with a chevron and move the switch there.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "'Delete all data' action",
      "issue": "A destructive, irreversible action is visually identical to Export and Tax settings, and sits in the same group — easy to tap by mistake.",
      "fix": "Move it into its own section below a 24px gap: `<List.Item title=\"Delete all data\" titleStyle={{color: theme.colors.error}} left={p => <List.Icon {...p} icon=\"trash-can-outline\" color={theme.colors.error}/>} onPress={openConfirm} />` with no chevron, and gate it behind a Paper `Dialog` with Cancel / `<Button textColor={theme.colors.error}>Delete</Button>`.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "Bottom tab bar",
      "issue": "Tab labels (Dashboard, Receipts, Mileage, Settings) are clipped at the bottom edge on phone — the bar does not account for the safe-area inset and its height is too small for icon + label.",
      "fix": "In the shared tab navigator options set `tabBarStyle={{height: 56 + insets.bottom, paddingTop: 8, paddingBottom: 8 + insets.bottom, backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface, borderTopColor: theme.colors.outlineVariant}}` using `useSafeAreaInsets()`, and `tabBarLabelStyle={{fontSize: 12, lineHeight: 16}}`.",
      "shared": true
    },
    {
      "element": "Section grouping / subheaders",
      "issue": "All six destinations sit in one flat run, so unrelated concerns (security, data, legal) read as one long undifferentiated list.",
      "fix": "Group into three sections with `<List.Subheader>` styled `theme.fonts.labelLarge` in `theme.colors.primary`, 24px top margin / 8px bottom: 'Security' (App lock), 'Data' (Tax settings, Export, Backup & restore, Delete all data), 'About' (View Terms and Privacy Policy). Item label 'View Terms and Privacy Policy' → 'Terms & Privacy Policy'.",
      "shared": false
    },
    {
      "element": "Screen header 'Settings'",
      "issue": "The title is oversized (≈34px bold) relative to the rest of the UI and uses ad‑hoc top padding, so it won't match other tabs; on desktop it sits flush with the 512px column with no breathing room.",
      "fix": "Use the shared `ScreenHeader` with `<Text variant=\"headlineMedium\">` (28/36) in `theme.colors.onSurface`, container padding `{paddingTop: 24, paddingBottom: 16, paddingHorizontal: 16}`, and have the screen body use the same 16px horizontal padding inside a `maxWidth: 640` centered container for desktop.",
      "shared": true
    }
  ]
}

