{
  "summary": "The app’s UI largely follows DESIGN.md and passes axe (0 violations) and Lighthouse accessibility (98) scores. All screens in the primary flow are present and navigation via the bottom tab bar and FAB works. However, several critical and medium‑severity gaps were found: the PolicyGate error state is missing (could block onboarding), backup‑passphrase validation is weak, CSV/PDF exports are vulnerable to injection, the web build lacks a CSP header, temporary backup files are never removed, photo picker accepts unbounded image sizes, the encryption key survives a full data‑reset, and a few components still use hard‑coded values or lack a visible focus outline on web. Addressing these issues will bring the product to a polished, secure, and fully spec‑compliant state.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing error view for the PolicyGate screen – the spec requires a full‑screen error with the copy \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" and a Retry button, but the component only shows loading and default states.",
      "fix": "Add an error branch that renders a centered view with the required copy and a retry action that re‑invokes the acceptance storage logic."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The loading state on PolicyGate does not display the required text \"Checking policy version…\"; only an ActivityIndicator is shown.",
      "fix": "Wrap the ActivityIndicator in a view that also renders a Text component with the exact copy, using the theme's bodyLarge style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup passphrase UI accepts any non‑empty string; there is no validation for minimum length (8 characters) or character‑class complexity as required by the security checklist.",
      "fix": "Add validation logic that checks length >= 8 and at least three of the four character classes (upper, lower, digit, symbol). Show HelperText errors and keep the \"Create backup\" button disabled until the policy is satisfied."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/exportCsv.ts",
      "issue": "CSV export concatenates raw user fields without sanitising leading characters, exposing the app to CSV/Formula injection (e.g., cells starting with =,+,-,@).",
      "fix": "Implement a sanitisation step that prefixes a single quote to any field that starts with =,+,-,@ or, simpler, wrap every field in double quotes and escape internal quotes using a CSV library like `csv-stringify`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/exportPdf.ts",
      "issue": "PDF export builds an HTML string by interpolating user‑provided data directly, opening the possibility of HTML injection in PDF viewers.",
      "fix": "Escape all user‑generated strings with an HTML‑escaping utility (e.g., `escape-html`) before inserting them into the template, or use a safe templating library that auto‑escapes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "public/index.html",
      "issue": "The web fallback does not include a Content‑Security‑Policy meta tag, leaving the page vulnerable to XSS if ever served on the web.",
      "fix": "Add a CSP meta tag (or configure the web server to send the header) restricting sources to `'self'` for scripts, styles, images, etc. Example: `<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:;\">`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/backup.ts",
      "issue": "After creating an encrypted backup the temporary file used for `expo-sharing` is never deleted, leaving the encrypted blob (and possible plaintext) on the device.",
      "fix": "Call `FileSystem.deleteAsync(tmpPath, { idempotent: true })` after a successful `shareAsync` and handle any errors; optionally overwrite the file before deletion for added safety."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/photoPicker.ts",
      "issue": "Receipt photo picker accepts arbitrarily large images; no size or resolution limit is enforced, which can exhaust device storage and degrade performance.",
      "fix": "Set `quality`/`allowsEditing` options on the picker, and after selection check `FileSystem.getInfoAsync` for file size. Reject or down‑scale images above a defined threshold (e.g., 5 MB or 2048 px width)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/dataReset.ts",
      "issue": "The \"Delete all data\" action wipes SQLite tables but does not delete the encryption key stored in SecureStore, leaving encrypted remnants potentially recoverable.",
      "fix": "When performing a full reset, also call `SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(KEY_NAME)` to remove the key, and optionally overwrite the database file."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No visible focus‑outline is applied for web when the button receives keyboard focus; users navigating via Tab cannot see which element is focused.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` CSS rule (or RNWeb style) that sets a 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline` to match the design token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Horizontal padding is hard‑coded as `paddingHorizontal: 16` dp instead of using `theme.spacing * 2` as defined in the layout spec.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded value with `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing * 2` (i.e., 16 dp) and pull the value from the theme to keep spacing consistent."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/*",
      "issue": "Several components use literal color values (e.g., `#FFFFFF`, `#0061A4`) instead of the exported design tokens, risking divergence from the palette.",
      "fix": "Replace all hard‑coded color literals with references to `theme.colors` (or CSS custom properties on web) and remove any unused color constants."
    }
  ]
}

