{
  "summary": "The built UI matches the DESIGN.md spec in almost every respect – all screens, core states (loading, empty, populated, error) are present, the bottom tab bar and FAB navigation work on both phone and desktop, and the Lighthouse & axe audits show excellent accessibility (98) and no violations. Design tokens are used for the majority of colors, spacing, and typography, and the layout respects the mobile‑first 390 dp viewport with no horizontal overflow. However, a few important details are missing or only partially implemented, leading to medium‑severity findings. These relate to form validation, security‑related sanitisation, and some optional‑web fallback behaviours. None of these break the primary user flow or make the app inaccessible, so no high‑severity UI‑blocking issues were detected.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Form validation does not display per‑field `HelperText` errors nor shift focus to the first invalid input, contrary to the spec which requires field‑level validation messages and focus management.",
      "fix": "Add validation logic that checks each required field, set the `error` prop on `FormField`, render a `HelperText` component with the appropriate message, and programmatically focus the first invalid input using refs."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The backup passphrase modal only checks for matching fields; it does not enforce the minimum‑length rule (≥ 8 characters) required by the design, and there is no UI feedback if the length requirement is not met.",
      "fix": "Validate the passphrase length on each change, display a `HelperText` error when < 8 characters, and keep the **Create backup** button disabled until both the length and matching constraints are satisfied."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/exportCsv.ts",
      "issue": "CSV export concatenates raw user input without sanitising leading characters (`=`, `+`, `-`, `@`), creating a CSV‑formula injection risk.",
      "fix": "Implement a sanitisation step that prefixes a single quote to any value starting with those characters, or wrap every field in double quotes and escape internal quotes before joining rows."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/exportPdf.ts",
      "issue": "PDF export builds an HTML string by interpolating user‑provided data directly, exposing the app to HTML injection attacks in PDF viewers.",
      "fix": "Escape all user‑supplied strings using an HTML‑escaping library (e.g., `escape-html`) before inserting them into the PDF template, and consider sanitising or stripping dangerous tags."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
