{
  "summary": "Re‑evaluated the earlier security findings after the latest code changes. CSV export and PDF export injection issues have been mitigated, and the vulnerable uuid dependency has been upgraded. All other previously reported issues remain open, and the high‑severity unpatched dependencies (braces, node‑forge) and other medium‑severity concerns (backup passphrase policy, web key storage, temp‑file cleanup, numeric validation, CSP header, image size limits, key persistence after data delete) still need remediation. No new security problems were discovered in the current snapshot.",
  "previous": [
    {
      "id": "high-csv-injection",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "Sanitisation of user‑provided fields added to CSV export; issue fixed, severity unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "high-pdf-html-injection",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "HTML‑escaped all user data before building the PDF template; issue fixed, severity unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-backup-passphrase-policy",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Backup UI still accepts any non‑empty passphrase; no complexity enforcement – remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-web-key-storage",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Web fallback still persists the encryption key in localStorage; no change – remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-temp-backup-file-deletion",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Temporary file created for expo‑sharing is not deleted after sharing; remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-input-validation-numeric",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Numeric inputs (amount, mileage, rates) still allow negatives, non‑numeric strings and overly large values; remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "deployment-csp-header",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Web fallback still lacks a CSP header/meta tag; remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-image-size-validation-2026-00001",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Photo picker accepts arbitrarily large images; no size/resolution limits – remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-key-persistence-after-data-delete",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Encryption key in expo‑secure‑store is not removed when the user chooses \"Delete all data\"; remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "high-deps-braces-2026-93687",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "Vulnerable `braces` v3.0.3 still present; no patched version available – remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "high-deps-node-forge-2026-85393",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "Vulnerable `node‑forge` v1.4.0 (transitive via expo‑crypto) still present; no patched version yet – remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-deps-sprintf-js-2026-97058",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "`sprintf‑js` v1.0.3 still present; no fix yet – remains open."
    },
    {
      "id": "medium-deps-uuid-2026-41907",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Dependency upgraded to uuid ^13.0.1 which contains the fix; issue resolved."
    }
  ],
  "findings": []
}

{
  "summary": "The app’s UI largely follows the DESIGN.md spec – all primary screens appear in the flow, the Lighthouse accessibility score is 98, axe reports no violations, and the layout is mobile‑first with proper padding and spacing. The design tokens are imported via the shared theme and the custom UI components wrap React‑Native‑Paper primitives. However, several important functional and security gaps remain. Critical issues include missing sanitisation for CSV export and HTML escaping for PDF export (both high‑severity injection risks) and vulnerable third‑party packages (braces, node‑forge). Medium‑severity concerns are missing input validation on numeric fields, weak backup‑passphrase enforcement, lack of CSP on the web build, leftover temporary backup files, unchecked image‑size limits, and incomplete key removal on full data wipe. These gaps could lead to data loss, user confusion, or security breaches and should be addressed before launch.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/lib/exportCsv.ts",
      "issue": "CSV export concatenates raw user fields without sanitisation, enabling CSV/Formula injection when a cell starts with =, +, - or @.",
      "fix": "Escape each field before joining rows – either prefix a single quote for dangerous leading characters or wrap all fields in double quotes and escape inner quotes. Implement a sanitizeCsvValue() helper and use it for every column."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/lib/exportPdf.ts",
      "issue": "PDF export builds an HTML string by interpolating user‑provided data directly, exposing the app to HTML injection/XSS in PDF viewers.",
      "fix": "HTML‑escape all dynamic values before inserting them into the PDF template (e.g., with the escape-html library) and consider whitelisting allowed characters only."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "package-lock.json",
      "issue": "The `braces` package (v3.0.3) has CVE‑2026‑93687 – a denial‑of‑service vulnerability via deeply nested regex patterns.",
      "fix": "Upgrade `braces` to a patched version (>= 3.0.4) or remove the dependency if it isn’t required. Run `npm update braces` and regenerate the lock‑file."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "package-lock.json",
      "issue": "`node‑forge` (v1.4.0) contains CVE‑2026‑85393 – RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature forgery, used transitively by expo‑crypto.",
      "fix": "Upgrade to `node‑forge` >= 1.5.0 or replace the crypto functionality with a vetted library such as the @noble/* suite. Update imports and re‑run tests."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Backup UI only checks that a passphrase is non‑empty; there is no enforcement of a minimum length or character‑class complexity.",
      "fix": "Add validation that requires at least 8 characters and at least three of the four character classes (upper, lower, digit, symbol). Show HelperText on failure and keep the Create button disabled until the policy is satisfied."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Numeric fields (amount, etc.) lack validation – negative numbers, non‑numeric strings and unreasonably large values can be entered, and the Save button may stay enabled.",
      "fix": "Validate amount on change: must be a number > 0 and below a sensible upper bound (e.g., 9 digits). Display a HelperText error and disable the Save button until the field validates."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Mileage fields have no comprehensive validation – miles can be negative or non‑numeric, purpose can be empty, and date may be missing.",
      "fix": "Add per‑field validation: miles numeric ≥ 0 with a max limit, purpose required, date required. Show HelperText errors and disable Save until all pass."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "public/index.html",
      "issue": "The optional web fallback does not include a Content‑Security‑Policy (CSP) meta tag or header, leaving the page vulnerable to script injection.",
      "fix": "Add a CSP meta tag (or configure the hosting server to send a CSP header) restricting sources to 'self' for scripts, styles, images, etc. Example: `<meta http-equiv=\"Content‑Security‑Policy\" content=\"default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:;\">`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/backup.ts",
      "issue": "After creating an encrypted backup, the temporary file used for expo‑sharing is never deleted, leaving residual data on the device.",
      "fix": "After a successful `Sharing.shareAsync` call, invoke `FileSystem.deleteAsync(tmpPath, { idempotent: true })` to securely remove the temporary file."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/photoPicker.ts",
      "issue": "Image picker accepts arbitrarily large photos; a malicious user could take extremely high‑resolution images that exhaust device storage.",
      "fix": "Set a maximum resolution/quality in the ImagePicker options (e.g., `quality: 0.8`, `maxWidth: 2048`, `maxHeight: 2048`). Also check the file size with `FileSystem.getInfoAsync` and reject files above a safe threshold."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/lib/dataReset.ts",
      "issue": "\"Delete all data\" clears the SQLite tables but does not delete the encryption key stored in SecureStore, so encrypted remnants could be recovered.",
      "fix": "When performing a full data wipe, also delete the key from SecureStore (e.g., `SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(KEY_NAME)`) and clear any in‑memory caches."
    }
  ]
}

